# Environment variables required for local Terraform development.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. If you have mise
# installed (https://mise.jdx.dev), it will load `.env` automatically
# when you `cd` into the repo. Otherwise, source it manually:
#   set -a && source .env && set +a
#
# DO NOT commit a populated .env file. It is gitignored on purpose.

# --- Terraform Cloud token (sensitive) ---
# Personal API token used to authenticate against the Terraform Cloud
# remote backend. Generate one at:
#   https://app.terraform.io/app/settings/tokens
# The remote workspace is `waldoibarra-com` in the `waldo-io` org:
#   https://app.terraform.io/app/waldo-io/workspaces/waldoibarra-com
TF_TOKEN_app_terraform_io=

# --- Notes on other configuration ---
# AWS credentials: provide via ~/.aws/credentials or standard AWS
# environment variables (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY).
#
# Terraform input variables:
#   - domain_name defaults to "waldoibarra.com" in vars.tf
#   - application defaults to "portfolio" in vars.tf
#   - Route 53 hosted zone is looked up automatically by domain name
#     via a data source — no TF_VAR_hosted_zone_id needed.
